  "worked_solution": "To graph the first inequality $y\\ge 3x,$ we draw the corresponding straight line $y=3x.$\n\n- Since we have a \"or equal to\" inequality, the line itself is included in the solution, so the line is solid.\n\n- The inequality refers to the $y$-values that are *greater than* or equal to those on the line, so we shade *above* the line.\n\nTo graph the second inequality $y>\\frac{1}{4}x,$ we draw the corresponding straight line $y=\\frac{1}{4}x.$\n\n- Since we have a strict inequality, the line itself is *not* included in the solution, so the line is dashed.\n\n- The inequality refers to the $y$-values that are *greater than*  those on the line, so we shade *above* the line.\n\nThe intersection of the solutions is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/15608503fc9aa3ffe20cd649cf2d0adab657a09961811c206a7bce16a34c9c2f.png)",
